{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":27958530,"ns":0,"title":"Virology Journal","revisions":[{"revid":1373069395,"parentid":1331375056,"minor":true,"timestamp":"2026-09-03T21:52:37Z","size":5307,"sha1":"fabbff696b2ab4f1e3987c4fdfe90b996892526c","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"{{distinguish|Virology (journal){{!}}''Virology'' (journal)}}\n{{Use dmy dates|date=December 2021}}\n{{Infobox journal\n| title = Virology Journal\n| cover = [[File:Headsquare.gif|140px]]\n| editor = [[Linfa Wang]]\n| discipline = [[Virology]]\n| abbreviation = Virol. J.\n| publisher = [[BioMed Central]]\n| country =\n| frequency = Rolling\n| history = 2004–present\n| openaccess = Yes\n| license = [[Creative Commons]] Attribution Generic 2.0\n| impact = 5.55\n| impact-year = 2021\n| website = http://www.virologyj.com\n| link1 = http://www.virologyj.com/articles/browse.asp\n| link1-name = Online access\n| link2 =\n| link2-name =\n| JSTOR =\n| OCLC = 56433791\n| LCCN =\n| CODEN =\n| ISSN = 1743-422X\n| eISSN =\n}}\n'''''Virology Journal''''' is an [[Open access (publishing)|open-access]] [[Peer review|peer-reviewed]] [[medical journal]] published by [[BioMed Central]]. It publishes research related to [[virus]]es and the prevention of [[infection|viral infection]] (including [[vaccine|vaccination]], the use of [[antiviral drug|antiviral agents]], and [[gene therapy]]). The journal was established in 2004 with Robert Garry ([[Tulane University]]) as founding [[editor-in-chief]] and has been edited by [[Linfa Wang]] since 2012. It aims to cover rapid communications amongst virologists.\n\n== Controversy ==\nOn 21 July 2010, ''Virology Journal'' published an article entitled \"Influenza or not influenza: Analysis of a case of high fever that happened 2000 years ago in Biblical time\", regarding the case of the mother-in-law of [[Saint Peter|Simon Peter]] who the Bible reports was cured by [[Jesus]]. The authors conclude that she was struck with [[influenza]].<ref>\n{{cite journal\n |author1=Kam LE Hon |author2=Pak C Ng |author3=Ting F Leung |year=2010\n |title=Influenza or not influenza: Analysis of a case of high fever that happened 2000 years ago in Biblical time\n |journal=Virology Journal\n |volume=7 |pages=169\n |doi=10.1186/1743-422X-7-169\n |pmc=2918564\n |pmid=20663162\n |issue=1\n |doi-access=free\n}}{{Retracted|doi=10.1186/1743-422X-7-190|pmid=20707907|http://retractionwatch.com/2010/08/12/the-shroud-of-retraction-virology-journal-withdraws-paper-about-whether-christ-cured-a-woman-with-the-flu/ ''Retraction Watch''|intentional=yes|doi-access=free}}</ref> This article created controversy amongst scientists, who decried the article from anywhere from \"truly bizarre\"<ref name=Aetiology>\n{{cite web\n |author=Tara C. Smith\n |date=10 August 2010\n |title=Biblical fever = influenza. You're kidding me, right?\n |url=https://scienceblogs.com/aetiology/2010/08/10/biblical-fever-influenza-youre\n |work=Aetiology\n |publisher=[[ScienceBlogs]]\n |access-date=2010-08-11\n}}</ref> to \"garbage\".<ref name=Pharyngula>\n{{cite web\n |author=[[PZ Myers]]\n |date=11 August 2010\n |title=But what if she had vapors, or an imbalance of humors? |url=http://scienceblogs.com/pharyngula/2010/08/but_what_if_she_had_vapors_or.php\n |work=[[Pharyngula (blog)|Pharyngula]]\n |publisher=[[ScienceBlogs]]\n |access-date=2010-08-11\n |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100815212432/http://scienceblogs.com/pharyngula/2010/08/but_what_if_she_had_vapors_or.php\n |archive-date=2010-08-15\n |url-status=dead\n}}</ref> The editor-in-chief of ''Virology Journal'' later apologized for the publication and announced that it would be retracted.<ref name=VJComments>\n{{cite journal\n |author=Robert Garry\n |title=Influenza or not influenza: Analysis of a case of high fever that happened 2000 years ago in Biblical time – Comments\n |journal=Virology Journal\n |date=21 July 2010\n |volume=7\n |issue=1\n |page=169\n |doi=10.1186/1743-422X-7-169\n |pmid=20663162\n |pmc=2918564\n |s2cid=8124033\n |doi-access=free\n }}{{Retracted|doi=10.1186/1743-422X-7-190|pmid=20707907|http://retractionwatch.com/2010/08/12/the-shroud-of-retraction-virology-journal-withdraws-paper-about-whether-christ-cured-a-woman-with-the-flu/ ''Retraction Watch''|intentional=yes|doi-access=free}}</ref> The article was retracted on 13 August 2010.<ref>\n{{cite journal\n |author1=Kam LE Hon |author2=Pak C Ng |author3=Ting F Leung |year=2010\n |title=Retraction: Influenza or not influenza: Analysis of a case of high fever that happened 2000 years ago in Biblical time\n |pmid=20707907\n |journal=Virology Journal\n |volume=7 |issue=1 |pages=190\n |doi=10.1186/1743-422X-7-190\n |pmc=2924865\n|doi-access=free }}</ref>\n\n== Abstracting and indexing ==\n''Virology Journal'' is abstracted and indexed in\n{{columns-list|colwidth=30em|\n*[[PubMed]]\n*[[PubMed Central]]\n*[[MEDLINE]]\n*[[Thomson Reuters]]\n*[[CAB International]]\n*[[Chemical Abstracts Service]]\n*[[EMBASE]]\n*[[Scopus]]\n*[[Current Contents]]\n}}\n\n== References ==\n{{Reflist}}\n\n== Further reading ==\n*{{cite journal\n |author=Robert F. Garry\n |year=2004\n |title=Virology on the Internet: the time is right for a new journal\n |journal=Virology Journal\n |volume=1 |page=1\n |doi=10.1186/1743-422X-1-1\n |pmc=524032\n |pmid=15507150\n |issue=1\n|doi-access=free\n }}\n\n== External links ==\n* {{Official website|http://www.virologyj.com/}}\n\n[[Category:BioMed Central academic journals]]\n[[Category:Open-access journals]]\n[[Category:Academic journals established in 2004]]\n[[Category:English-language journals]]\n[[Category:Virology]]\n[[Category:Creative Commons-licensed journals]]\n[[Category:Virology journals]]\n[[Category:Continuous journals]]"}}}],"contentmodel":"wikitext","pagelanguage":"en","pagelanguagehtmlcode":"en","pagelanguagedir":"ltr","touched":"2026-11-17T19:44:48Z","lastrevid":1373069395,"length":5307}]}}